Name: jmap_require_accountid
Type: SWITCH
Default-Value: 0
Last-Modified: UNRELEASED

If enabled, a JMAP method call that omits the "accountId" argument (or
gives a null or non-string value) is rejected with an "invalidArguments"
error, as RFC 8620 requires of every method other than Core/echo.  If not
enabled (the default), a missing or null "accountId" is taken to mean the
authenticated user's own account, which is what Cyrus has always done and
what some deployed clients rely on.
